  "_notes": {
    "abbreviations": "Bulgarian abbreviations are written out in full: МПС = véhicule à moteur, ППС = véhicule, ПТП = accident de la circulation, ЗДвП = loi sur la circulation routière, ППЗДвП = règlement d'application de la loi sur la circulation routière, МВР = ministère de l'Intérieur, КАТ = police de la route, ИААА = Agence exécutive « Administration automobile », ДВГ = moteur à combustion interne, ТОЛ = péage. Standard abbreviations: ЕС = UE, ЕО = CE, ЕКМТ/СЕМТ = CEMT, ТИР = TIR. Latin acronyms stay as written (ABS, ESP, ASR, BUS, IRU, LED, ADR, CMR, TIR).",
    "legal_distinctions": "изпреварване = dépassement (dépasser), заобикаляне = contournement (contourner), разминаване = croisement (croiser). престой = arrêt (Code de la route sense: immobilisation pour la montée/descente ou le chargement/déchargement); паркиране = stationnement; спиране in the generic traffic sense = immobilisation / s'arrêter; спиране in the braking sense = freinage / freiner. ППС = véhicule, МПС = véhicule à moteur (Vienna Convention sense, excludes mopeds), автомобил = automobile (f.), лек автомобил = voiture particulière, товарен автомобил = véhicule de transport de marchandises. прекъсване = pause, почивка = temps de repos (Regulation (EC) No 561/2006, FR text).",
    "mass": "допустима максимална маса = masse maximale autorisée (EU legal French, Directive 2006/126/EC; this is the French PTAC). It is never abbreviated, so that 'masse maximale autorisée de l'ensemble' (combination) stays correct.",
    "excess": "превишавам (a speed or value) = excéder, never 'dépasser', to keep 'dépasser' exclusively for overtaking (изпреварвам).",
    "entitlement": "правоспособност за категория X = permis de catégorie X (titulaire du permis de catégorie X); правоспособност without a category = droit de conduire; без правоспособност = sans permis; загуба на правоспособност = perte du droit de conduire; свидетелство за управление на МПС = permis de conduire (the document).",
    "answers": "Yes/no-type answers in lower case: да/не = oui/non; правилно/неправилно = correct/incorrect; вярно/невярно = vrai/faux; разрешено/забранено = autorisé/interdit (agreement follows the subject when the stem requires it).",
    "address": "The candidate is addressed with 'vous'. Как ще постъпите? = Comment agirez-vous ? ; Какво ще направите? = Que ferez-vous ?",
    "modality": "длъжен е = est tenu de; трябва = doit; задължително = obligatoirement; може = peut; има право = a le droit de; разрешено е = est autorisé; забранено е = est interdit; не се разрешава = n'est pas autorisé; препоръчително е = il est recommandé de.",
    "punctuation": "French typography: U+00A0 (no-break space) before ? : ; ! and inside « » (written as the JSON escape \\u00a0). Quotation marks are « … » for every Bulgarian quote style („…“, “…”, \"…\"). Apostrophe: straight U+0027. Questions keep '?', stems ending in ':' keep ':' and answers continue them in lower case.",
    "numbers_units": "Decimal comma as in Bulgarian. Thousands grouping mirrors the Bulgarian (a space in the source becomes U+00A0). SI symbols are kept; Cyrillic symbols become Latin SI symbols (км/ч = km/h, м = m, см = cm, мм = mm, кг = kg, т = t). Unit words stay words (тона = tonnes, метра = mètres). A no-break space U+00A0 separates a number from its unit symbol and from % and ‰. 24-hour clock. Dates keep their digits ('12.12.24г.' = '12.12.24').",
    "categories": "Licence categories always in Latin letters (AM, A1, A2, A, B1, B, BE, C1, C1E, C, CE, D1, D1E, D, DE); national categories Tkt, Ttb, Ttm. Picture labels use the Latin look-alike letter (А = A, В = B).",
    "citations": "чл. 157, ал. 4 ЗДвП = art. 157, al. 4, de la loi sur la circulation routière (Bulgarian 'алинея' = French 'alinéa').",
    "carriageway": "The question bank treats 'пътно платно' and 'платно за движение' as different legal terms (iaaa-5230: 'Пътното платно включва: банкетите, платното за движение, островите…'; part 08: 'Граница на платното за движение … отделя платното за движение от другите конструктивни елементи на пътното платно'). Therefore платно за движение = chaussée and пътно платно = plate-forme routière (the French road-engineering term for chaussée(s) + accotements + terre-plein/îlots), everywhere.",
    "roads": "автомобилен път (the signed road class for motor vehicles: white car on blue, Vienna Convention sign E,6a; closed to mopeds, tractors and bicycles; no U-turns or reversing) = route à accès réglementé, the name of that sign in France (C107, white car on blue; reviewer's decision, replacing the Vienna Convention / Belgian name 'route pour automobiles', which French learners do not know as a sign name and could read as a generic road); скоростен път (expressway, 120 km/h for B) = route express; автомагистрала = autoroute; населено място = agglomération; жилищна зона = zone résidentielle (Vienna Convention FR term).",
    "ui": "Interface (ui-strings.json): formal 'vous'; buttons in the infinitive as in the French Android system apps (Fermer, Annuler, Réessayer, Continuer); titles are nouns. Шофьорски изпит (app name) = Examen du code; Изпитен тест = Examen blanc, тест = test; упражнение / упражнявам = entraînement / s'entraîner; Отметки / отбелязани = Favoris; Напредък = Progrès; Настройки = Paramètres; вариант = variante, случай (the candidate's case) = situation; зачетен / незачетен = validée / non validée; предаване на теста = remise du test; научени = apprises. ИААА is written in full (Agence exécutive « Administration automobile »); the Latin acronym (IAAA) appears only in the legal notices, after the full name. The category blurbs for C, C1 and CE say 'camion(s)': in French law a camion is a goods vehicle over 3.5 t, which is exactly what these categories cover (the questions keep 'véhicule de transport de marchandises', see legal_distinctions). Plurals use the French CLDR forms one / many / other; 'many' (exact millions) puts 'de' before a noun ('%1$d de points'); strings whose quantity is the total use the pattern 'X sur Y points' or a label ('Questions apprises : X sur Y') so that every form agrees."
  }
}
